ddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[2195,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2197,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2191,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[2193,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[2198,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[2194,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[2192,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[2196,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[2107,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[646,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1723,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1241,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1366,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[401,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[294,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1242,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1367,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[296,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1244,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1805,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1368,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[400,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[1112,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[295,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1243,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[398,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1110,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1109,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[397,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[1111,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[399,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[2099,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[446,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[161,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[211,"`CardGroup` uses grid navigation: Tab enters or leaves, arrow keys move between Cards, and Space\nchanges selection. Enter activates row actions or links. Choose selection or `onAction`;\ncombining them prevents pointer selection."],[1910,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[280,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[350,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[368,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[346,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[361,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1847,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[437,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[447,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[448,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[439,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[2044,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1176,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[739,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[742,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[738,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[740,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[741,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[743,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1503,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[486,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1653,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[564,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[660,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1644,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1652,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[1019,"`Enter/Space`"],[60,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[444,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[608,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[833,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[573,"`Escape`"],[961,"`Escape`"],[1021,"`Escape`"],[1852,"`Escape`"],[645,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[2177,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[747,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2135,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[662,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[451,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[821,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[850,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[2027,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[663,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2105,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[880,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2104,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[915,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[159,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[489,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[954,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[949,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1175,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1902,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1572,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when ne